    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44085" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sextĭlĭus</span></b> , i,
			m.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sextĭlĭa</span></b> , ae,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
				name of a Roman</i> gens: C. Sextilius Rufus, Cass. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Cic. Ep. Fam. 12, 13, 4</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">13, 48</span></i> tit.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sextilia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Vit. 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 2, 64</span></i>. —Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sextĭlĭānus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>named from a Sextilius</i>: pira, Cloat. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Macr. S. 2, 15 <i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
